Run the create-from-image qemu-img calls as the service user

Patch 0001 flips the NFS driver's forced-root `qemu-img info`. Two more
forced-root calls sit above the driver on the same create-from-image
path, and neither of them goes through it.

`CreateVolumeFromSpecTask._create_from_image_cache_or_download`
(cinder/volume/flows/manager/create_volume.py) inspects the image it has
just downloaded with `image_utils.qemu_img_info(tmp_image)`, whose
`run_as_root` defaults to True. `fetch_verify_image`
(cinder/image/image_utils.py) inspects the same file through
`get_qemu_data(image_id, has_meta, format_raw, dest, True)`, which passes
the flag positionally and offers no way to ask for anything else. In both
cases the file is the temporary copy the service itself wrote into
`image_conversion_dir`, owned by uid 42424 and reachable by nobody else,
so reading it as root gains no privilege the process does not already
have.

Under the restricted posture of #979 decision D3 there is no root to
fall back to: the root helper is `sudo cinder-rootwrap` with no sudoers
entry, and every such call fails with `sudo: The "no new privileges"
flag is set`. The two calls fail differently, and both are worth fixing:

* The manager call raises that ProcessExecutionError uncaught, so every
  create-from-image ends in `error` status.
* The `fetch_verify_image` call swallows it. `get_qemu_data` reads a
  failing `qemu-img` as "qemu-img is not installed", returns None for a
  raw image and skips the backing-file and data-file checks the function
  exists for (bugs 1996188 and 2059809), and raises ImageUnacceptable for
  every other disk format.

The #985 lab measured the flow with the `sudo` shim of evidence section
(a.4) in place, which answers every forced-root call in the tree, so only
the driver's own call was left to attribute and patch 0001 was sized for
it alone. Without the shim both calls surface: on the first Tempest run
of PR #995, 14 of 192 tests failed on each release, and every failure
created a volume from an image or a snapshot.

Three upstream unit tests pin the `fetch_verify_image` argument and move
with it, in cinder/tests/unit/test_image_utils.py:
`TestVerifyImage.test_defaults`,
`TestFetchToVolumeFormat.test_no_qemu_img_fetch_verify_image`, and the
first expected call of `TestFetchToVolumeFormat.test_temporary_images`.
The other two calls that last test expects come from
`fetch_to_volume_format`, which still takes the flag from its caller, so
they stay True. No upstream test pins the manager call, so the
create_volume.py hunk needs no test hunk. The image build runs the
upstream unit suite, which is where a missing one shows up.

tests/container-images/verify_cinder.sh asserts both call sites against
the built image, beside the assertion for patch 0001.

Applies to cinder 28.0.0 (2026.1).

Upstream status: not yet proposed.

